| `shell.enabled` | boolean | `true` | `true`, `false`; a generated project takes the copier answer `shell` | `scripts/shell_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `shell.enabled` row | `false` makes `make lint-sh`, `make fmt-sh`, `make fmt-check-sh` and `make test-sh` say `shell.enabled is false` on stdout and exit 0 having run no tool, so a project with no shell needs none of the tools. It switches the tools only: check_O and `tests/integration/test_exit_gate.py` judge every shell script either way, and false excuses a project with no shell script from `shell.no_scripts` in that exit gate. Absent, each target writes `[using default] shell.enabled = true` to stderr. | choosing a tool: `shell.linter`, `shell.formatter`, `shell.test_runner` | always |
